    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Outer Wilds",
    "description": "This wallpaper is based on the amazing space exploration game '[url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/753640/Outer_Wilds]Outer Wilds[/url]'\r\n\r\n\r\n[h3]☑️Settings and Features[/h3]\r\nThere is a second scene that can be enabled but it will be a spoiler to anyone who hasn't played the first few hours of the game🌞Play the game first! It's great!\r\n\r\nAnimations such as the campfire and the aurora can be disabled.\r\n\r\nStars have audio responsive animations which can be [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussion/2984500160/3884975231690052382/]tuned via sliders[/url] as well as disabled by unchecking either [I]Audio recording[/I] or [I]Audio Responsive[/I] (unchecking one vs the other will have a different look to the stars).\r\n\r\nThere are particle elements that can interact with your mouse\r\n\r\n[h3]🎨Key Art by [url=https://www.ianjacobson.com/Outer-Wilds]Ian Jacobson[/url][/h3]\r\n\r\n[h3]🎶Music by [url=https://soundcloud.com/andrewprahlow]Andrew Prahlow[/url][/h3]\r\n[olist]\r\n[*] [spoiler]End Times[/spoiler]\r\n[*] [spoiler]Travelers[/spoiler][/olist]\r\n\r\nPlaying '[url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/753640/Outer_Wilds]Outer Wilds[/url]' and ruminating on events after each session finally gave me the inspiration to create my first wallpaper ::o\r\n\r\n::)",
